
## 3. `docs/requirements/product-requirements.md`

```markdown
# Campus Hostel Product Requirements

## 1. Product Overview

Campus Hostel is a web platform for students searching for accommodation around a university.

The MVP will serve one university campus but will be designed to support additional universities in future versions.

## 2. Product Goal

Allow students to discover hostels, view reliable accommodation information, and submit booking requests without visiting every hostel physically.

## 3. Stakeholders

| Stakeholder | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| Business owner | Defines business requirements and validates completed features |
| Sunday Jime | Designs, develops, tests, and documents the platform |
| Students | Search for hostels and submit booking requests |
| Hostel managers | Provide accurate hostel and availability information |
| Administrators | Manage listings, rooms, and bookings |

## 4. User Roles

### 4.1 Visitor

A visitor can:

- Visit the platform without logging in
- Browse published hostel listings
- Search and filter hostels
- View hostel details
- View photos and videos
- View room types, prices, and amenities

A visitor cannot:

- Submit a booking
- Access student pages
- Access administrator pages

### 4.2 Student

A student can:

- Register an account
- Log in and log out
- Manage basic profile information
- Browse hostel listings
- Submit a booking request
- View personal bookings
- Track booking status
- Cancel a booking when permitted

A student cannot:

- Access another student’s bookings
- Create or edit hostel listings
- Approve booking requests
- Access administrator pages

### 4.3 Administrator

An administrator can:

- Log in securely
- Create hostel listings
- Edit hostel information
- Upload hostel photos and videos
- Add room types
- Set room prices
- Update room availability
- Publish or hide listings
- View student accounts
- View booking requests
- Approve or reject bookings

## 5. Functional Requirements

### FR-001: Browse Hostels

The system shall display all published hostel listings.

### FR-002: Search Hostels

The system shall allow users to search for hostels by name.

### FR-003: Filter Hostels

The system shall allow users to filter hostels by:

- Price range
- Gender restriction
- Room type
- Amenities
- Availability

### FR-004: View Hostel Details

The system shall display:

- Hostel name
- Description
- Address
- Distance from campus
- Photos
- Videos
- Amenities
- Rules
- Room types
- Prices
- Availability

### FR-005: Student Registration

The system shall allow students to register using valid personal information.

### FR-006: Authentication

The system shall allow registered students and administrators to log in securely.

### FR-007: Submit Booking Request

The system shall allow an authenticated student to select a room type and submit a booking request.

### FR-008: Booking Status

A booking shall have one of the following statuses:

- `PENDING`
- `APPROVED`
- `REJECTED`
- `CANCELLED`

### FR-009: Booking History

The system shall allow students to view their booking history.

### FR-010: Hostel Management

The system shall allow administrators to create, update, publish, and hide hostel listings.

### FR-011: Room Management

The system shall allow administrators to manage room types, prices, quantities, and availability.

### FR-012: Booking Management

The system shall allow administrators to approve or reject booking requests.

## 6. Initial Booking Workflow

1. A student logs in.
2. The student selects a hostel.
3. The student selects a room type.
4. The student submits a booking request.
5. The booking receives a unique reference.
6. The booking status becomes `PENDING`.
7. An administrator checks availability.
8. The administrator approves or rejects the request.
9. The student sees the updated booking status.

## 7. Non-Functional Requirements

### Security

- Passwords must never be stored as plain text.
- Administrator pages must be protected.
- Students must not access other students’ data.
- Environment secrets must not be committed to GitHub.
- Inputs must be validated on the frontend and backend.

### Performance

- Public pages should load quickly.
- Images should be compressed and optimized.
- Database queries should use appropriate indexes.
- Hostel listings should support pagination as the platform grows.

### Usability

- The interface must be mobile-responsive.
- Forms must display useful validation messages.
- Navigation must be clear.
- Important actions must provide visible feedback.

### Accessibility

- Images must include alternative text.
- Forms must have labels.
- Keyboard navigation must be supported.
- Text must have readable colour contrast.

### Reliability

- Errors must be handled without crashing the application.
- Booking records must not be lost.
- Database relationships must be protected with constraints.
- Important administrator actions should eventually be logged.

### Maintainability

- Frontend and backend responsibilities must remain separated.
- Reusable logic must not be unnecessarily duplicated.
- Important features must be documented.
- Naming conventions must remain consistent.

## 8. MVP Exclusions

The MVP will not initially include:

- Payment processing
- Automatic refunds
- Multiple universities
- Hostel-owner dashboards
- Reviews and ratings
- Live chat
- SMS notifications
- Native mobile applications
- AI recommendations

## 9. Success Criteria

The MVP is successful when:

- Visitors can browse hostel listings.
- Visitors can inspect room information and media.
- Students can create accounts and submit booking requests.
- Administrators can manage hostels and room types.
- Administrators can approve or reject bookings.
- Students can track their booking status.
- The platform works on mobile and desktop devices.

## 10. Pending Business Decisions

- University name and location
- Whether students book an entire room or a room type
- Rental period: monthly, semester, session, or yearly
- How hostel availability will be verified
- Payment provider
- Full payment versus deposit
- Cancellation policy
- Refund policy
- Platform service fee